% BULK OPS -- the whole-array (APL-style) operator battery of
% test/unit/bulk_ops.sis, given a driver and exact references.
%
% The unit file says of itself: "All functions are parse-only stubs; the bodies
% just invoke the new primitives so the parser / AST builder get exercised."  So
% it proved the operators PARSE and nothing about what they compute.  Nothing
% needed rewriting for the dope-vector model -- it was already written in
% array_dv -- it needed a main and a reference.
%
% Measured before writing this: of the ~50 primitives the unit file names, 35
% lower to C++ and compile.  All 35 are exercised here and agree with the
% standard meaning of the operator.  Three did NOT when this file was first
% written -- SCAN dropped the total (af35d42) and ARGMAX/ARGMIN answered 0 for
% every input -- and were left out rather than pinned wrong until fixed.  What
% is still missing has no C lowering at all and is listed at the bottom.
%
% Worth knowing: TAKE, DROP, TILE, CONCAT, MAP and SCAN do NOT lower to a named
% runtime helper -- the backend generates a loop for each.  Their behaviour is
% therefore a property of the LOWERING, which is exactly what a value test pins
% and a parse test cannot.
%
% The eight ELEMENTWISE forms below (a+b .. a*n) could not be returned from a
% multi-output function until 34f06a7: the broadcast lowering's BROADCAST_ERROR
% panic edge shares port numbers with the data ports, and infer_types typed
% result port 1 from it, truncating a dope to int32_t at the ABI.  Keeping them
% here alongside everything else is what pins that.

define main

type ai = array_dv[integer];
type ar = array_dv[real];
type ab = array_dv[boolean];

% the helpers the higher-order primitives take as their function argument
function add_i (u, v : integer returns integer)  u + v   end function
function neg_i (u    : integer returns integer)  0 - u   end function
function sub_i (u, v : integer returns integer)  u - v   end function
function win_sum (w : ai returns integer)        SUM(w)  end function

function main( a, b : ai;              % rank-1 integers, equal length
               msk : ab;               % rank-1 mask, same length (NOT `m`:
                                       % names are case-insensitive, so `m`
                                       % would collide with the matrix `M`)
               x, y : ar;              % rank-1 reals, same length
               M : ar;                 % rank-2 reals, for PERMUTE
               P, Q : ar;              % rank-2 reals, for INNERPRODUCT
               n, lo, hi, k, z, f : integer
      returns
        ai, ai, ai, ai,                % elementwise + - * unary-
        ab, ab,                        % elementwise = <
        ai, ai,                        % scalar broadcast + *
        integer, integer, integer, integer,   % SUM PRODUCT LEAST GREATEST
        integer, integer,                     % ranged SUM, ranged LEAST
        ai, integer, integer, ai, ai,   % MAP FOLDL FOLDR SCAN SCAN(-)
        ai, ai, ai, ai,                % TAKE DROP ROTATE REVERSE
        ai, ai, integer, integer,      % COMPRESS SORT ARGMAX ARGMIN
        ai, ar,                        % NONZERO WHERE
        ai, ai, ai, ai,                % CONCAT TILE PAD PAD-with-fill
        ai, ar, ar )                   % STENCIL INNERPRODUCT PERMUTE
  a + b,
  a - b,
  a * b,
  -a,
  a = b,
  a < b,
  a + n,
  a * n,
  SUM(a),
  PRODUCT(a),
  LEAST(a),
  GREATEST(a),
  SUM(a, lo, hi),
  LEAST(a, lo, hi),
  MAP(neg_i, a),
  FOLDL(add_i, z, a),
  FOLDR(add_i, z, a),
  SCAN(add_i, a),
  SCAN(sub_i, a),      % non-commutative: pins LEFT association
  TAKE(a, n),
  DROP(a, n),
  ROTATE(a, k),
  REVERSE(a),
  COMPRESS(msk, a),
  SORT(a),
  ARGMAX(a),
  ARGMIN(a),
  NONZERO(a),
  WHERE(msk, x, y),
  CONCAT(a, b),
  TILE(a, n),
  PAD(a, lo, hi),
  PAD(a, lo, hi, f),
  STENCIL(win_sum, a, 3),
  INNERPRODUCT(P, Q),
  PERMUTE(M, 1, 0)
end function

% NOT COVERED -- no C lowering at all today ("Unsupported IF1 Simple node
% symbol"), so they cannot be given a value test yet:
%   ANY, ALL, MEAN, VARIANCE, STDDEV, NORM   -- statistical / boolean folds
%   CUMSUM, CUMPROD                          -- cumulative
%   GRADE_UP / GRADE_DOWN (= ARGSORT)        -- DV_GRADE_UP / DV_GRADE_DOWN
%   RAVEL (= FLATTEN_DV), SQUEEZE, EXPAND    -- shape-changing
%   SUM/PRODUCT/LEAST/GREATEST(a, axis)      -- REDUCE_AXIS
% and OUTERPRODUCT, which fails differently: its function argument reaches the
% backend as a FUNCTION_TYPE with no C mapping.  MAP, FOLDL, FOLDR, SCAN and
% STENCIL also take function arguments and DO lower, so that gap is specific to
% OUTERPRODUCT's path, not to higher-order ops in general.
